# ============================================================
# J.A.R.V.I.S. — Environment Variables
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your keys
# ============================================================

# ── LLM API Keys (REQUIRED) ──────────────────────────────────

# Google Gemini — reserved for complex reasoning, vision, and optional embeddings
# Get from: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Groq — default chat/reasoning provider plus fast Whisper STT
# Get from: https://console.groq.com/keys
GROQ_API_KEY=


# ── Google Cloud OAuth (OPTIONAL — for Calendar & Gmail) ─────
#
# JARVIS uses OAuth 2.0 (NOT API keys) for Google Calendar and Gmail.
# You do NOT put credentials here. Instead, follow these steps:
#
# 1. Go to https://console.cloud.google.com/
# 2. Create a new project (or use an existing one)
# 3. Enable the APIs you want:
#    - Google Calendar API:  APIs & Services → Library → search "Google Calendar API" → Enable
#    - Gmail API:            APIs & Services → Library → search "Gmail API" → Enable
#
# 4. Create OAuth 2.0 credentials:
#    - APIs & Services → Credentials → "+ CREATE CREDENTIALS" → "OAuth client ID"
#    - If prompted, configure the OAuth consent screen:
#        • User Type: External
#        • App name: JARVIS
#        • Add your email as a Test User
#    - Application type: Desktop app
#    - Name: JARVIS Desktop
#    - Click Create → DOWNLOAD JSON
#
# 5. Place the downloaded file as credentials.json in:
#    - %APPDATA%\JARVIS\credentials.json           (recommended)
#
#    Or set JARVIS_GOOGLE_CREDENTIALS_PATH to its absolute path. The legacy
#    src\jarvis\config\credentials.json location is supported for migration,
#    but should not be used for new setups because it sits inside the source tree.
#
# 6. First time you ask JARVIS about your calendar or email, it will
#    open your browser for Google sign-in. Click "Allow".
#    Refreshable Gmail and Calendar tokens are saved under %APPDATA%\JARVIS,
#    so application updates do not break access.
#
# Required OAuth Scopes (automatically requested):
#   - https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar        (read + write calendar events)
#   - https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.readonly   (read emails)
#   - https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.compose    (create drafts and send approved drafts)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
